@*
    Concurrency view (task 11.5) — renders duration-aware concurrency over a single day stacked by
    queue, with a dashed worker-capacity reference line, and flags the buckets whose concurrency
    strictly exceeds capacity with a distinct indicator (Req 4.8, 4.9).

    The concurrency itself is computed server-side by the pure ConcurrencyAnalyzer (surfaced through
    HeatmapService.GetConcurrencyAsync) and handed to this component as a ConcurrencyResult; this view
    only maps that result into the `window.heatmapCharts.renderConcurrency` model and manages the JS
    chart lifecycle, following the same IJSRuntime interop pattern as the other heatmap views and the
    existing analytics charts.

    Phase 1 note: the renderer's model carries an `adhoc` baseline layer and a `cron` layer. The cron
    layer is populated from the per-queue concurrency series (aggregated into the single cron layer).
    In Combined mode (JobClass == "Combined", task 16.4 / Req 19.1, 19.2) the per-slot ad-hoc baseline
    from AdHocBaselinePerSlot — derived by the caller from the Demand_Profile — is emitted as a
    distinct `adhoc` layer; the JS renderer stacks `adhoc + cron` and compares the combined total to
    capacity when flagging over-capacity buckets and drawing the capacity line. In Cron/Ad-hoc mode the
    ad-hoc layer is suppressed.
*@
@namespace a2n.Hangfire.Dashboard.Components.Pages.Heatmap
@using a2n.Hangfire.Dashboard.Models

@if (!HasData)
{
    <EmptyState Icon="activity"
                Message="No concurrency to display."
                Subtitle="No projected fires fall on the selected day, so nothing runs concurrently." />
}
else
{
    <div class="heatmap-concurrency">
        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-3 mb-2 small text-body-secondary">
            <span>
                <i class="bi bi-graph-up-arrow me-1"></i>Peak
                <strong class="text-body">@Result.PeakConcurrency</strong> concurrent@(PeakTimeText is null ? string.Empty : $" at {PeakTimeText}")
            </span>
            <span>Capacity <strong class="text-body">@Capacity</strong></span>
            @if (Result.OverCapacitySlotCount > 0)
            {
                <span class="text-danger">
                    <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle-fill me-1"></i>@Result.OverCapacitySlotCount minute(s) over capacity
                </span>
            }
            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(DayLabel))
            {
                <span>Day <strong class="text-body">@DayLabel</strong></span>
            }
        </div>
        <div class="heatmap-concurrency-canvas" style="position:relative;height:340px;">
            <canvas id="@_canvasId"
                    aria-label="Concurrent jobs over the day stacked by queue, with a worker-capacity reference line"></canvas>
        </div>
    </div>
}
